---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: claude-memory-governance
covers: subtree
purpose: >
  The native agent-memory substrate: one durable fact per topic file, recallable through
  frontmatter (title: + description: <= 160 chars — the projected hook). MEMORY.md is a
  GENERATED projection of that frontmatter (memory-index-projector.py, PostToolUse-wired),
  never a hand-maintained index — the 2026-07-02 context-leak (26KB hand-index > harness
  load cap, truncated load) is the scar tissue. Durable knowledge GRADUATES outward to its
  managed home (subject-routing.yaml); native memory stays light.
rules:
  - id: memory-frontmatter-at-birth
    policy: memory-frontmatter-at-birth@1
  - id: memory-index-is-generated
    class: dispatch
    when: { write: "MEMORY.md" }
    dedupe-of: .claude/scripts/memory-kit/memory-index-projector.py
    parameters:
      dispatch-agent: librarian
      dispatch-prompt: >
        Check whether this MEMORY.md edit belongs in a topic file's title/description frontmatter
        and identify the exact source file or projector command that should own it. Report the
        correction to the editing agent without editing files; do not pause the current task.
    why: >
      MEMORY.md is GENERATED — hand edits are overwritten on the next projection. Put the
      change in the topic file's title:/description: frontmatter, then run
      `python3 .claude/scripts/memory-kit/memory-index-projector.py --apply` (the
      PostToolUse hook also re-projects after every memory write).
---

# .claude/memory — native memory, projection-disciplined

One fact per topic file; the file's `title:` + `description:` frontmatter IS its recall
surface (projected into MEMORY.md, which is generated — see the rules above). Budget
escalation is wired: over-soft-budget and per-file hook violations land in
`.claude/memory-kit/memory-index-drift.json`, which feeds the `cleanup:` pressure gate
toward the memory-stasis-loop. Real budget relief is population work — umbrella entries
(`index: false` on folded members), graduation to stories/managed homes — never index
hand-editing. Designed as a thin declarative layer that lifts into the brit/eprfs
projection substrate unchanged.
